É16 dekemvri, v razgara na surovata irlandska zima. Fina snezhna pokrivka se stele nad Niugreindzh, nevinno biala, skrivashcha ot pogleda chernata zemia. Niakolko dushi sa se s'brali okolo mal'k, priasno otvoren grob. Edin ot tiakh protiaga r'ka, za da dokosne onova, koeto lezhi na d'noto. Arkheolozhkata Ilon Baui chesto pris'stva na razravianeto na drevni grobove, no nikoga pred ochite i ne se e otkrivala tolkova uzhasiavashcha gledka. Tia s izumlenie ustanoviava kak e prichinena nechiia sm'rt - ochite sa izvadeni, g'rloto e preriazano. Koi bi mog'l da zasluzhi tak'v bezslaven i potresavashch krai? I togava zapochvat ubiistvata. Edin po edin onezi, koito sa bili s Ilon krai drevniia grob, namirat sm'rtta si po s'shchiia strakhovit nachin - s izvadeni ochi, preriazani g'rla i usti, nat'pkani s's zelenika. Tr'gvaiki po sledite na ritualnite ubiistva, arkheolozhkata razbira, che v chernata zemia sa zaroveni ne samo trupove, no i nepodozirani drevni taini. I niakoi e gotov da stigne do krai, za da ne b'dat razkriti."à

Ö
If you think computer security has improved in recent years, The Myths of Securitywill shake you out of your complacency. Longtime security professional John Viega, formerly Chief Security Architect at McAfee, reports on the sorry state of the industry, and offers concrete suggestions for professionals and individuals confronting the issue.
Why is security so bad? With many more people online than just a few years ago, there are more attackers -- and they're truly motivated. Attacks are sophisticated, subtle, and harder to detect than ever. But, as Viega notes, few people take the time to understand the situation and protect themselves accordingly. This book tells you:
Why it's easier for bad guys to "own" your computer than you think Why anti-virus software doesn't work well -- and one simple way to fix it Whether Apple OS X is more secure than Windows What Windows needs to do better How to make strong authentication pervasive Why patch management is so bad Whether there's anything you can do about identity theft Five easy steps for fixing application security, and more Provocative, insightful, and always controversial, The Myths of Securitynot only addresses IT professionals who deal with security issues, but also speaks to Mac and PC users who spend time online."¢
üBuck, a sturdy crossbreed canine (half St. Bernard, half Shepherd), is a dog born to luxury and raised in a sheltered Californian home. But then he is kidnapped and sold to be a sled dog in the harsh and frozen Yukon Territory. Passed from master to master, Buck embarks on an extraordinary journey, proving his unbreakable spirit...
First published in 1903, The Call of the Wildis regarded as Jack London's masterpiece. Based on London's experiences as a gold prospector in the Canadian wilderness and his ideas about nature and the struggle for existence, The Call of the Wildis a tale about unbreakable spirit and the fight for survival in the frozen Alaskan Klondike."©
¶,,Kalevala" e epicheska poema, koiato finlandets't Elias L'onrot s'stavia prez 19 vek na osnovata na folklora na Finlandiia i Kareliia. Priznata e za finlandski natsionalen epos i traditsionno smiatana za edno ot nai-znachimite proizvedeniia v'v finlandskata literatura. Na ,,Kalevala" se pripisva chast ot prinosa za natsionalno probuzhdane, dovelo do otvoiuvaneto na nezavisimostta na Finlandiia ot Rusiia prez 1917 g.
Poemata se s'stoi ot 22 795 strofi, razdeleni v 50 runi (glavi). Dumata ,,Kalevala" mozhe da se razbira kato ,,zemite na Kaleva"."´
®The story of the bus--and the passengers who changed history. Like all buses in Montgomery, Alabama, in the 1950s, bus #2857 was segregated: white passengers sat in the front and black passengers sat in the back. Bus #2857 was an ordinary public bus until a woman named Rosa Parks, who had just put in a long day as a seamstress, refused to give up her seat to a white passenger. Her arrest sparked the Montgomery Bus Boycott, a major event in the Civil Rights moment, led by a young minister named Dr. Martin Luther King, Jr. For 382 days, black passengers chose to walk rather than ride the buses in Montgomery. From the streets of Montgomery to its present home in the Henry Ford Museum, here is the remarkable story, a recipient of the Crystal Kite Award, of a bus and the passengers who changed history."¨
©Bruta e Izbraniia. K'm nego se obr'shcha Bog, makar i vremenno v'v formata na kostenurka.
Bruta e prostovato momche, no iska da s'bori edna ogromna i korumpirana ts'rkva, da predotvrati uzhasna sveshchena voina, iska mir, spravedlivost i bratska obich. Iska Inkvizitsiiata da spre da go izm'chva sega, molia vi...
No nai-veche tova, koeto naistina iska, poveche ot vsichko ostanalo, e negoviia Bog da Si Izbere Niakoi Drug..."≠
™Fent'zi, nauchna fantastika, khor'r, komediia, literaturen variant na film na Bratia Marks? Kakto i da narechem prochutite "Istorii za kronopi i fami", niama da sgreshim. Po-dobre prosto gi prochetete. Za da ostanete zavinagi v plen na "velikiia kronop" ot Arzhentina, "koito, po dumite na Markes, karashe vsichki da go obiknat"...
" Nikoi ne mozhe da prerazkazhe istoriite na Kortasar - vsiaka ot tiakh se s'stoi ot opredeleni dumi v opredelen red, ako se opitame, shche zagubim neshcho mnogo tsenno..."
Khorkhe Luis Borkhes
Khulio Kortasar (1914-1984), arzhentinski intelektualets i pisatel, zaedno s Khorkhe Luis Borkhes, e edno ot nai-golemite imena na arzhentinskata literatura. Stil't mu e nepovtorim, mozhe da b'de opredelen kato eksperimentatorski, na granitsata na fantastikata i khaliutsinatsiiata..."∏
µRoman't "S'rtsata na trimata" otkriva nova nasoka v tvorchestvoto na Dzhek London. "Polozhitelno nikoga dosega ne s'm pisal neshcho podobno; pochti polozhitelno e, che nikoga veche ne shche napisha neshcho podobno - otbeliazva toi. - I ni nai-malko ne se svenia da zaiavia kolko s'm gord, che s'm go napisal.""π
∂Conceived as a fairly serious guide to amateur boating on the Thames in 1889, Jerome K. Jerome's best-known novel ended up as a hilarious account of the misadventures of three friends and a dog as they attempt to relax and enjoy themselves amid unreliable weather forecasts, imaginary illnesses, repellent cooking, and an unopenable can of pineapple chunks.Three Men in a Boat was a terrific success for its author, and a surprisingly accurate portrayal of the age. George, Harris, and J., the narrator, were entertaining representatives of the new middle class, seeking to escape the dreary world of offices and desks during weekend trips out into the countryside. Jerome's heroes proved so popular that he brought them back for an equally picaresque bicycle tour of Germany, an adventure recorded in Three Men on the Bummel. The new Introduction by Jeremy Lewis describes the social context of the two books and the remarkable life of their author."∆
√V tazi kniga obobshchavam provezhdani v prod'lzhenie na poveche ot 30 godini izsledvaniia v'rkhu faktorite, koito karat dobri khora da stavat slugi na zloto. Tazi transformatsiia na choveshkiia kharakter naricham ,,Efekta Lutsifer", narechen na liubimiia angel na Boga, koito gubi blagorazpolozhenieto mu i v kraina smetka se prevr'shcha v Satana.
Vmesto da predlagam religiozen analiz obache, predstaviam psikhologichesko obiasnenie na tova kak obiknoveni khora poniakoga stavat zli i izv'rshvat neopisuemi deistviia. Kato chast ot tozi razkaz v ,,Efekt't Lutsifer" za pr'v p't razkrivam tsialata istoriia zad Stanfordskiia zatvornicheski eksperiment - stanalo veche klasika izsledvane, koeto provedokh prez 1971 g. V nego obiknoveni studenti biakha razpredeleni na sluchaen printsip da igraiat rolite na nadziratel ili na zatvornik za dve sedmitsi v simuliran zatvor, no nadziratelite b'rzo stanakha tolkova brutalni, che eksperiment't triabvashe da b'de prekraten samo sled shest dni.
Kak i zashcho se os'shchestvi tazi transformatsiia i kak se s'otnasia k'm neotdavnashni s'bitiia kato maltretiraneto na zatvornitsi v Abu Graib v Irak? Ednakvo vazhno e kakvo ni kazva tia za choveshkata priroda i kakvo ni podskazva za efektivnite nachini za predotvratiavane na takiva zloupotrebi v b'deshche.
Posledvaite me v tova p'tuvane, koeto poet't Milt'n bi mog'l da opishe kato prevr'shchane na mraka v neshcho vidimo. Makar chesto da e trudno da se chete za zloto ot p'rvo litse, triabva da razberem negovite prichini, za da go ud'rzhim i da go transformirame chrez m'dri resheniia i novatorski obshchi deistviia. Vs'shchnost spored men dnes niama po-speshna zadacha pred nas.
Filip Zimbardo
pocheten profesor,
Stanfordski universitet"«

