Spechelila milioni chitateli po sveta, nagrazhdavana i vsepriznata za edin ot v'rkhovete v'v fantastikata, ,,Igrata na End'r" e sred znakovite knigi na poslednite desetiletiia.
Nadkhv'rlil ramkite na zhanra, roman't e filosofski traktat za obshchuvaneto i choveshkite vzaimootnosheniia, samotata i moralniia izbor.
V b'deshcheto Zemiata e napadnata ot po-razvita tsivilizatsiia i edva se spasiava ot unishchozhenie. V otchaianieto si Mezhdunarodniiat flot obuchava svr'khinteligentni detsa za voinitsi, za da izpolzva neobremenenite im ot v'zrastta sposobnosti sreshchu nashestvenitsite. Izkliuchitelno talantliv i intuitivno razbirashch okolniia sviat, 6-godishniiat End'r shche se okazhe edinstvenata nadezhda na chovechestvoto za spasenie.
Svet't na Ors'n Skot Kard e mnogoplastov, postroen s logicheska pretsiznost i proniknovena psikhologiia, nasiten s d'lbok smis'l i naselen s iarki personazhi.
Blizka po dukh s ,,1984" i ,,Prekrasniiat nov sviat", ,,Igrata na End'r" e p'rva kniga ot legendarnata saga na Kard. Roman't i negovoto prod'lzhenie ,,Govoritelia na m'rtvite" sa nositeli na nagradite ,,Khiugo" i ,,Nebiula", a avtor't e edinstveniiat, pechelil nai-prestizhnite otlichiia za fantastika v dve poredni godini. Prez 2013 g. predstoi filmovata premiera na ,,Igrata na End'r"s uchastieto na Kharis'n Ford, Ben Kingsli i Eisa B't'rfild."—
ŒStanislav Lem -- nai-izt'knatiiat predstavitel na polskata nauchno-fantastichna literatura -- se radva na shiroka populiarnost sred chitatelite i osobeno sred mladezhta. Slavata na negovite proizvedeniia otdavna prekrachi granitsite na Polsha. Negovite romani ,,Astronavti", ,,Solaris", ,,Magelanoviiat oblak" i niakoi ot nai-khubavite mu razkazi sa prevedeni na mnogo evropeiski ezitsi.
Povestta ,,Nepobedimiiat" e edin ot v'rkhovete v negovoto tvorchestvo. Tia predstavia izv'nredno interesen i izp'lnen s narastvashcho naprezhenie razkaz za prezhiviavaniiata na grupa piloti i izsledovateli na Kosmosa. Ekipazh't na kosmicheskiia korab ,,Nepobedimiiat" popada na m'rtva planeta, ostava tam, za da provede nauchni prouchvaniia, i prezhiviava neobiknoveni prikliucheniia.
Eto kakvo pishe samiiat Lem za svoeto proizvedenie: ,,Nepobedimiiat" mozhe da se schita za povest za kosmicheski prikliucheniia, izp'lnena s tainstveni opasnosti i strelba. I tova shche b'de do izvestna stepen viarno... no ,,Nepobedimiiat" e khudozhestveno proizvedenie, v koeto stava duma predi vsichko za... za stremezha da se dokazhe, che kolkoto i da sa mog'shchi prilaganite ot choveka tekhnicheski sredstva, ne e izkliucheno da se iaviat situatsii, kogato tsialata tazi atomno-kibernetichna tekhnika se okazva nedostat'chna i na choveka se nalaga da zastane sam -- litse sreshchu litse s iavlenie, protiv koeto negovite avtomati i mashini shche sa bezsilni... Otnachalo na izpitanie se podlaga avtomatichnata tekhnika, a sled neinoto porazhenie -- tvorets't na tazi tekhnika, koito izliza... ot skhvatkata nepobedim. I togava ne na gigantskiia kosmicheski korab, a na obezor'zheniia chovek shche prinadlezhi imeto, koeto ednovremenno e i nazvanie na tazi povest.""‹
ŸIstoriia za izgubeniia rai i chetiri choveshki s'dbi. Izgubenata nevinnost na Kashmir e i pogubenata chistota na edna mladezhka liubov, podkrepena ot obshchnostta v'preki religioznite razlichiia v edna s'vremenna istoriia za Romeo i Zhulieta. Lichnata drama na Shalimar klouna i tragediiata na Kashmir go atakuvat pochti ednovremenno i prevr'shchat edin blagoroden mlad m'zh v bezskrupulen i zhestok terorist. Razkaz za d'lboka i fatalna liubov, unishchozhena ot mimoletno pl'tsko uvlechenie - drama, koiato ni prenasia ot Kaliforniia prez Frantsiia i Angliia do Kashmir - edin ne tolkova izguben, kolkoto unishchozhen rai. Shed'ov'r, koito obediniava nai-burnite choveshki strasti i nai-sm'rtonosnite konflikti na nasheto vreme."›
⁄Sred grobnitsata t'mna na skr'bta,
k'deto men S'dbata zatochi me,
k'deto l'ch ne trepva i Noshchta
e gospodarkata s's stranno ime,
a az - khudozhnik na nasmeshliv bog,
os'den da risuvam v'rkhu mraka;
k'deto sam kato gotvach zhestok
s'rtseto si varia, che glad me chaka,
poniakoga prist'pva nezhna, krotka
videlina - t'i kakto dnes probliasna!
I dokato izrasne tia - edna! -
po lekata i iztochna pokhodka
poznavam svoita gostenka prekrasna:
makar i cherna - vse pak svetlina."‡
›Git is the version control system developed by Linus Torvalds for Linux kernel development. It took the open source world by storm since its inception in 2005, and is used by small development shops and giants like Google, Red Hat, and IBM, and of course many open source projects. A book by Git experts to turn you into a Git expert Introduces the world of distributed version control Shows how to build a Git development workflow
What you'll learn Use Git as a programmer or a project leader. Become a fluent Git user. Use distributed features of Git to the full. Acquire the ability to insert Git in the development workflow. Migrate programming projects from other SCMs to Git. Learn how to extend Git.
Who is this book for?
This book is for all open source developers: you are bound to encounter it somewhere in the course of your working life. Proprietary software developers will appreciate Git's enormous scalability, since it is used for the Linux project, which comprises thousands of developers and testers. About the Apress Pro Series
The Apress Pro series books are practical, professional tutorials to keep you on and moving up the professional ladder.
You have gotten the job, now you need to hone your skills in these tough competitive times. The Apress Pro series expands your skills and expertise in exactly the areas you need. Master the content of a Pro book, and you will always be able to get the job done in a professional development project. Written by experts in their field, Pro series books from Apress give you the hard-won solutions to problems you will face in your professional programming career."Á
‰V tezi istorii grupa alpinisti ziapat oblatsite, dokato pochistvat prozortsite na visokite sgradi; edin m'zh chete znatsite v golemiia grad kato lichni poslaniia; bezraboten filosof nabliudava kak krotko nazriavat revoliutsiite. ,,Visoka oblachnost" s'bira razkazi, pisani prez poslednite shest godini, koito ni razkhozhdat ot ,,Zhenskiia pazar" v Sofiia do tsent'ra na Tirana, prez krainite kvartali i pekarnite za arabski sladkishi do visokite planini, k'deto oblatsite si pochivat."Ë

