"There is no deeper mark of being a Jew than exile"
In 1654, fifteen hundred Jews were driven from a Dutch colony in Brazil by a conquering Portuguese army. A fleet of sixteen ships transported the Jews back to Europe. However, one ship got lost in a storm. Drifting alone in the Atlantic, the ship was captured by pirates who brought the Jews to New Amsterdam. Penniless and unwelcome there, the refugees struggled to survive the wilderness of North America and the hostility of those seeking to control it.
One young refugee, Benjamin Vieira, works in the fur trade along the North River before being captured by a Mohawk warrior. After a daring escape, he makes his way east to New England where he takes refuge with the powerful Narragansett tribe. Benjamin believes a Jew must make his home wherever he is able. But tribal elders disagree. They contend Benjamin must live among his own people, Jewish merchants who have settled in Newport, Rhode Island. But Benjamin's life in the colonies is soon threatened by a bloody war between the English colonists and the Native Americans.
And Benjamin doesn't know which side he is on.
Set against the backdrop of the first Jewish settlement in North America in 1654 and King Philip's War from 1675-1676, Legend of the Dead is a story about the transformation of the New World and one young man's attempt to carve his place within it."Î
ËZhritsi v khramovete na Shumer i Mesopotamiia, pornai i kheteri v Drevna G'rtsiia, zoni v bibleiskiia Izrail, "svobodni" zheni v Dreven Rim, khomoseksualni orgii v drevniia sviat, razkaiali se greshnitsi, prev'rnati v svetitsi, kitaiski nalozhnitsi i iaponski geishi, voinishki bludnitsi i ulichni prostitutki v srednovekovna Evropa, sk'pi kurtizanki i kralski favoritki, momicheta ot viktorianskite bordei i ot salonite na Diviia zapad, kokotki i demimondenki ot Belepok, "beli robini" v Latinska Amerika i cherni "vtori s'prugi" v Afrika, svoboden seks v Polineziia, devadasi i ganiki v Indiia, prostitutki ot voinishki bordei prez dvete svetovni voini, koreiski "momicheta za raztukha", "germanski momicheta", kolg'rli...
Niakolko khiliadi godini istoriia na chovechestvoto i niakolko khiliadi godini istoriia na platenata liubov. Edna neveroiatna kniga, s'brala na stranitsite si ogromen broi fakti i iliustratsii za intimniia zhivot na choveka ot zarazhdaneto na negovata tsivilizatsiia do dnes."Ú
ÔSobstvena sm'rte mashchabna kniga. Lesna za chetene i pochti neizcherpaema. Sledva klasicheski metod: za nai-golemite neshcha govori s nai-prostite dumi. V'preki obichta si k'm razgovorniia ezik avtor't ne se poddava na izkushenieto na prekaleno oprosteniia nachin na izraziavane, ne se opitva da skrie naprimer, che pritezhava izvestna meditsinska nachetenost, che e veshch v oblastta na filosofskite poniatiia. I vse pak knigata ne e nauchnopopuliaren ili spetsializiran filosofski trud, a grandiozna prozaicheska poema. Dava ni onova, koeto i nai-dobriiat nauchen trud ne e v s'stoianie, a samo poeziiata mozhe da dade. - Vilfrid Vigand ,,Frankfurter Algemaine Tsaitung"
Sobstvena sm'rte razkaz't na edin goliam pisatel za opita sled sm'rtta. - Internet-spisanie ,,Litera"
Razt'rsvashch razkaz na chovek, prezhivial sobstvenata si sm'rt, za da se zav'rne k'm sveta na zhivite."Ù
ÒV kratkiia si zhivot Boris Vian (1920-1959) e bil inzhener i izobretatel, muzikant, avtor na pesni i pevets, stsenarist, dramaturg i akt'or, poet, prevodach i romanist. Liriz'm, siurrealiz'm i absurdiz'm se s'chetavat v negovite tvorbi, koito vzriviavat deistvitelnostta, ot'rsvat ia ot vsiakakva delnichnost i ia preizgrazhdat - fantasmagorichna, groteskna i zhestoka."	
